1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 f5 { The Latvian Gambit: a King's Gambit with reversed colours, a tempo down. }
3. Nxe5 { [%name 3.Nxe5 Main Line] }
( 3. Bc4 { [%name 3.Bc4] }
  3... fxe4 4. Nxe5 d5 { Hitting the bishop and building a pawn centre. }
  5. Qh5+ g6 6. Nxg6 Nf6 { Not 6...hxg6?? 7.Qxh8: the queen must retreat and block the attack. }
  7. Qe5+ Be7 8. Bb5+ c6 9. Nxe7 Qxe7 10. Qxe7+ Kxe7 { Black is fine: the c6 pawn hits b5 and the centre pawns are strong. } )
3... Qf6 { Hitting the knight and preparing ...fxe4 with pressure on the f-file. }
4. d4 d6 { Kicking the knight out of the centre. }
5. Nc4 fxe4 { Black now has a pawn on e4 and open lines on the f-file. }
6. Nc3 Qg6 { Hitting g2 and supporting the e4 pawn. }
7. f3 exf3 8. Qxf3 Nf6 { Development first: the king is a bit loose, but the pieces come out quickly. } *
